1) Conducting immediate rescue efforts for victims who are in dangerous conditions for their safety;
2) Providing referrals according to the needs of victims;
3) Providing counseling and support from family; 4) Treating child victims of economic and/or sexual exploitation humanely in accordance with the dignity and rights of children; 5) Providing a sense of security and protection for child victims of economic and/or sexual exploitation from media coverage; and 6) Providing rehabilitation and social reintegration services.

